{"title":"Sigma notation","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Sigma_notation&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p><p><b>Sigma notation</b>, also known as <i>summation notation</i>, provides a method for writing long, complicated, sometimes <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Infinite\" title=\"Infinite\">infinite</a> sums neatly and compactly.  Besides being easier to write than the explicit sum, sigma notation is also useful in that it shows the general form of each addend.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Definition\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Definition</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Description\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Description</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Properties\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Properties</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Examples\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Examples</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Definition\">Definition</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sigma_notation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Definition\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For any integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/3/2c3c3b257a6ed04ad40a382504e92231a48bc45c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\leq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> and any function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/3/df321a16c05c7d678128914f4147490710908e35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> defined on the integers, we write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/2/f123da29b5ca4914fcef03454ff609185c3cd328.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=m}^n a(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"64\" height=\"48\" /> for the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/5/ed517f7ce1a1ac5ae48ec95f1621b979b3e5ec42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(m)+a(m+1)+a(m+2)+\\ldots+a(n-1)+a(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"413\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sigma_notation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Description\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's first use an example to demonstrate how to use the notation.  Consider the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/5/145098512686e622db9b5850eedd592dff31e78f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+10+15+20+25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"170\" height=\"14\" />.  We'll denote the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sequence\" title=\"Sequence\">sequence</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea4d576937a04ec200b1037fc8ee33e8f744cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> where k is the number of terms being summed.  We want to rewrite the sum so that each term is in terms of its number k in the sequence.  <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factoring\" title=\"Factoring\">Factoring</a>, we get, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c5a8f95e02070bbcc825bd004695d79be8a9118.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+10+15+20+25=5(1+2+3+4+5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />.  Now, we see that each term is five times it's number in the sequence k; that is, as k ranges from 1 to 5, each term can be written as 5k.  This sum is written in summation notation as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/0/bf0a1caad98e73138c837087c0cd85c54f064ee8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^5 5k=5+10+15+20+25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"242\" height=\"50\" />.  In this case, 1 is the lower limit of summation, the number the index of summation k starts the sum with, and ends with the upper limit of summation 5.  One way to remember the terms is to note that the lower limit of summation is written <i>under</i> the sigma and the <i>upper</i> one is written above the sigma. Another example would be the summation of 1 to 10 which is 55\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Properties\">Properties</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sigma_notation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Properties\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For any constant c and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Finite\" title=\"Finite\">finite</a> (or <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Absolutely_convergent&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Absolutely convergent (page does not exist)\">absolutely convergent</a>) <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Series\" title=\"Series\">series</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea4d576937a04ec200b1037fc8ee33e8f744cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6bdec4394870e8a713538ce428bea9d41c8775f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, \n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/6/b46b2b7ebcd2821cb2668f87799af2567a55076e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_a^b c = c(b-a+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"152\" height=\"51\" /></li></ul>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d39f9067c9c54f212b23128a0943ced268da14b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum ca_k = c\\sum a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"138\" height=\"31\" /></li></ul>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec650105a516132a53bd689f6f7372548bb6ce57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum (a_k + b_k) = \\sum a_k + \\sum b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"232\" height=\"25\" /></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Examples\">Examples</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sigma_notation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Examples\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/2/f72aaddefc47397c25df6595f7b1f070db6d8998.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i = 33}^{56} 1 = 1 + 1 + \\ldots + 1 + 1 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"253\" height=\"50\" /></li></ul>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/7/1c7d6f32b03326b19b5462016dd510a61f88fabb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i = 1}^{\\infty} \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^i = \\dfrac{1}{2} + \\dfrac{1}{4} + \\dfrac{1}{8} + \\dfrac{1}{16} + \\ldots = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"304\" height=\"53\" /></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sigma_notation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Convergence&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Convergence (page does not exist)\">Convergence</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Greek_alphabet\" title=\"Greek alphabet\">Greek alphabet</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometric_sequence\" title=\"Geometric sequence\">Geometric sequence</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017185230\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.660 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 113/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 283/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3303/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.373      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.373      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3411:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017185230 and revision id 282121. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}